                <pb facs="0282" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg208"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 5.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Morrison to Mr. Portman.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Central Bank of Western India,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama, Japan,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 29, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your letter of yesterday’s date, with enclosure for the manager of the Oriental
                    Bank Corporation, requesting him to hold to my order the sum of two hundred and
                    fifty thousand dollars, ($250,000.)</p>
                <p>In accordance with the terms of your letter now. under acknowledgment, I beg to
                    hand you herewith six sets of bills, aggregating £56,770 16s. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">8d.</hi> sterling, and also memorandum of account and
                    particulars of said bills, the receipt of which please acknowledge.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <p>For the Central Bank of Western India,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. MORRISON, <hi rendition="#italic">Agent in
                    Yokohama.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. L. C. Portman,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Chargé d’ Affaires of the United States in
                            Japan.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
